## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 1.6.1 using npm
- Updated package.json with the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json to reflect the new package and its dependencies

#### 2. Root Layout Integration (src/app/layout.tsx)
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Integrated the `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag within the ThemeProvider
- Placed it alongside the existing `<SpeedInsights />` component for consistency

### Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`), which is the correct approach for Next.js App Router projects. The component is placed:
- Inside the `<body>` tag
- Within the `<ThemeProvider>` component
- After the `{children}` content and other utility components

This ensures that analytics will be tracked across all pages of the application.

### Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ Package installed successfully using npm
2. ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
3. ✅ Linter verified with no errors introduced by our changes (`npx eslint src/app/layout.tsx`)
4. ✅ Lock file (package-lock.json) updated appropriately

### Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

### Notes

- The project uses npm as its package manager
- The implementation follows Next.js App Router best practices
- The Analytics component is positioned consistently with the existing SpeedInsights component
- Pre-existing linting errors in other files were not addressed as they are unrelated to this implementation
